# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0014512> (PURA-related severe neonatal hypotonia-seizures-encephalopathy syndrome due to a point mutation)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Orphanet:438216") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0014512> "A rare, genetic neurological disease in which the cause of the disease is a point mutation in the PURA gene. It is typically characterized by neonatal hypotonia, respiratory and feeding difficulties, global development delay (often with nonverbal and frequently non-ambulatory progression) and myopathic facies. Other frequently present features include seizures (or seizure-like episodes), visual impairment and encephalopathy.")
