# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0014885> (Hermansky-Pudlak syndrome 10)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26744459") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30472485") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40028/") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7437-8060") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0014885> "Any Hermansky-Pudlak syndrome in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the AP3D1 gene disrupts AP‑3–dependent trafficking to lysosome‑related organelles, including melanosomes and platelet dense granules. Alongside oculocutaneous albinism and a platelet‑type bleeding diathesis, affected individuals develop early‑onset immunodeficiency and severe neurologic impairment (e.g., profound developmental delay and refractory seizures). Additional findings can include interstitial lung disease and hepatosplenomegaly.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000233> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0014885> "https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9994"^^xsd:anyURI)
